#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Stephen A. Phillips|chapter=The Visa|title=From Moscow with Love|location=Pittsburgh, Pa.|publisher=[[w:Dorrance Publishing Company|Dorrance Publishing Co.]]|page=57|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=1xmwZ9PZcvcC&pg=PA57|isbn=978-1-4349-0120-0|passage=But how could she ever meet him since he was half way around the world, a Visa was $175, and the plane trip to Moscow was $298. After all, she only made $90 a month. {{...}} '''Net'''! '''Net'''! '''Net'''! She cried and buried her head into her pillow. '''Net'''! '''Net'''! '''Net'''! She spoke the muffled words into her pillow as she hit her fist upon the bed.}}
